{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["And he saw, and behold, a ram — passing before him." "Afterwards, caught in the thicket by its horns — that is: afterwards he saw the ram as it passed by, caught in the thicket of the forest. He reasoned in his heart: this angel has surely come by the mission of the Holy One, blessed be He, and has provided me this ram in place of my son; therefore it is caught in the thicket, so that I can take it and offer it. And similarly: ״ושרים אחר נוגנים״; ״ושבו העבים אחר הגשם״; and afterwards: ״ובא הגשם״; and similarly ״ואחר באו משה ואהרן״ — all of them mean 'afterwards.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {1 "The three unaddressed biblical quotations are rendered verbatim without addresses, as Rashbam cites them; they illustrate the adverbial use of אחר meaning 'afterwards' (1 Samuel 18:10 / Exodus 9:33–34 / Exodus 5:20 respectively)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:44:48.759497125Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}